-- Legacy data import from the previous Sijill app (Netlify backup 2026-07-27).
-- Ids are deterministic UUIDv5 values so this migration is idempotent and
-- foreign keys resolve without lookups. Every insert is guarded by
-- "on conflict do nothing" so it cannot clobber rows already in the DB.
--
-- Deliberately NOT imported (see the import notes in the PR):
--   * employees          - no employee rows at all. The source stored PINs
--                          in plaintext, so rather than import locked
--                          accounts the staff list is re-entered through
--                          the UI. Nothing here references employee(id):
--                          asset.custodian_employee_id is left null.
--   * images/attachments - 5.9 MB of base64 blobs belong in object storage,
--                          not in a migration; re-upload via the UI.
--   * need/maintenance requests - transactional history with dangling item
--                          references; not worth carrying over.
--
-- The third name is NOT imported. This file previously carried Urdu
-- translations of every name; the app's third language is Hindi, so those
-- were dropped rather than fed into name_hi. Imported rows get name_ar and
-- name_en only, and name_hi stays null until someone fills it in through
-- the UI (the auto-translate button on each name form does it).
--
-- Numbered 68, not 61: production's Flyway history is already past 62 and
-- outOfOrder is off, so a lower version would abort startup. It therefore
-- runs after V66, which renamed name_ur to name_hi.


